1. File & Project Management
Command	Description
ls	List files and directories
cd	Change directory
mkdir project_name	Create new project directory
rm file.cpp	Remove a file
rm -r build/	Remove a directory recursively
cp source.cpp dest.cpp	Copy files
mv old.cpp new.cpp	Rename or move files
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Compilation & Building
Command	Description
g++ main.cpp -o main	Compile a single file using g++
g++ -Wall -Wextra file.cpp	Compile with warnings enabled
g++ -std=c++17 main.cpp -o main	Specify C++ standard
make	Use Makefile to build a project
cmake .	Generate build files with CMake
cmake --build build_dir/	Build using CMake
ninja	Faster alternative build system (requires build.ninja)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Running & Testing
Command	Description
./main	Run compiled program
valgrind ./main	Check for memory leaks
time ./main	Measure execution time
gdb ./main	Launch debugger
lldb ./main	Use LLDB debugger (macOS, LLVM)
./test_suite	Run unit tests (if you set them up with GoogleTest, Catch2, etc.)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. Debugging & Inspection
Command	Description
g++ -g main.cpp -o main	Compile with debug symbols
gdb ./main	Debug with GDB
strace ./main	Trace system calls
lsof	List open files (good for debugging file handles)
nm main	List symbols from object files or executables
objdump -d main	Disassemble compiled binary
readelf -a main	Inspect ELF file details
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. Code Navigation & Editing
Command	Description
vim main.cpp	Edit with Vim
nano main.cpp	Edit with Nano
emacs main.cpp	Edit with Emacs
ctags -R .	Generate tags for source code navigation
cscope -R	Code browser for large codebases
grep "main"	Search for "main" in files
grep -r "ClassName" .	Recursive grep through project
find . -name "*.cpp"	Find all .cpp files recursively
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. Package Management
Command	Description
sudo apt install g++	Install g++ (Debian/Ubuntu)
sudo yum install gcc-c++	Install g++ (RedHat/CentOS)
sudo pacman -S gcc	Install gcc/g++ (Arch)
brew install gcc	Install gcc on macOS via Homebrew
vcpkg install <lib>	Install C++ libraries with vcpkg
conan install .	Install dependencies using Conan
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7. Documentation & Help
Command	Description
man g++	Manual page for the g++ compiler
g++ --help	Command-line help for g++
info g++	GNU info page for g++
cppreference.com	(Online) Detailed C++ standard reference

